To: linux-sh@vger.kernel.org

Recently patchwork has been brought up on kernel.org with various
projects tied in. The linux-sh list has also been added, so all patches
sent to the list will automatically be fed in to patchwork. Folks that
are curious about the status of patches can get a general overview there,
which should also help to make sure that stuff aimed at future merge
windows that have merge dependencies aren't overlooked.

More information on patchwork (including a client for listing and
fetching from the patch queue) can be found at:

	http://ozlabs.org/~jk/projects/patchwork

The SH queue is located here:

	http://patchwork.kernel.org/project/linux-sh/list/
